; Self-tests for the CHC solver: parse + solve a graded suite of hand-written linear-LIA
; HORN problems (safe + unsafe + out-of-fragment) and assert the verdict.  Wired into
; `make chc-test`.  Exits nonzero on any mismatch (soundness: a wrong safe/unsafe is a
; hard failure; unknown where a definite answer was expected is a soft miss, reported but
; not failing, since v1 is incomplete).

(executable
 (name chc_test)
 (modules chc_test)
 (libraries oxsmt_chc))

; Direct equality-premise interpolation consumer. The Makefile enables the dark equality
; path; the executable requires a checked interpolant to be admitted by the CHC loop.
(executable
 (name chc_interp_test)
 (modules chc_interp_test)
 (libraries oxsmt_chc))
